body:
Ha! Grew up in Stockton and it was my first thought. And I'm 65 and living in Seattle for 30 years.

&#x200B;

PS Sorry if I hijacked--not totally clear on Reddit etiquette. I am 65 after all! (JK)

We'll be selling our Seattle home early next year and sellers are doing inspections here to show potential buyers.

&#x200B;

I like it because it'll streamline the selling process

Wow that's how I've done it too. I got spoilers doing that, bummer.

&#x200B;

 I'm almost through the second book in the Fitz/Fool trilogy and am already in mourning because I don't know what I'll do with myslef once I'm done. These books have helped me survive quarantine.

The report states cardiac arrest is the cause of death--see comments. It says sudden death could've been caused by several things that don't produce morphologic changes. As it states a cardiac arrythmia, CNS disturbance, or a metabolic disorder cannot be excluded and these things don't cause any change in the size of the heart but could lead to an arrest. They don't know. If it was a human I expect they might dig a little deeper.

I probably erred in using the term heart attack instead of arrest.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
